{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_h6tcfrszdvhjvfeem2uthbo6pnunkvkwk55mjd5znxofjx6d2b7a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01RYQ4c7e5G1VCWHXbNpvDmP","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-CLiksb/translated_rust/tests/common/mod.rs","old_string":"/// Run `exe` against a stdin that **never reaches end-of-file**: a background\n/// thread writes `pattern` in a loop until the child goes away.\n///\n/// `scanf` reads lazily, so the C program finishes as soon as its two\n/// conversions are done. A translation that slurps all of stdin first would hang\n/// here (or exhaust memory), which is why this returns `Err(elapsed)` on timeout\n/// instead of blocking the suite forever.\npub fn run_unbounded(\n    exe: &Path,\n    pattern: &[u8],\n    timeout: std::time::Duration,\n) -> Result<(Outcome, std::time::Duration), std::time::Duration> {\n    let mut child = Command::new(exe)\n        .stdin(Stdio::piped())\n        .stdout(Stdio::piped())\n        .stderr(Stdio::piped())\n        .spawn()\n        .unwrap_or_else(|e| panic!(\"spawn {exe:?}: {e}\"));\n\n    let mut sink = child.stdin.take().expect(\"piped stdin\");\n    let block: Vec<u8> = pattern.repeat(4096 / pattern.len().max(1) + 1);\n    let feeder = std::thread::spawn(move || {\n        // Stops as soon as the reader is gone (EPIPE).\n        while sink.write_all(&block).is_ok() {}\n    });\n\n    let start = std::time::Instant::now();\n    let status = loop {\n        match child.try_wait().expect(\"try_wait\") {\n            Some(s) => break s,\n            None => {\n                if start.elapsed() > timeout {\n                    let _ = child.kill();\n                    let _ = child.wait();\n                    let _ = feeder.join();\n                    return Err(start.elapsed());\n                }\n                std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(2));\n            }\n        }\n    };\n    let elapsed = start.elapsed();\n\n    let mut stdout = Vec::new();\n    let mut stderr = Vec::new();\n    if let Some(mut s) = child.stdout.take() {\n        let _ = s.read_to_end(&mut stdout);\n    }\n    if let Some(mut s) = child.stderr.take() {\n        let _ = s.read_to_end(&mut stderr);\n    }\n    let _ = feeder.join();\n\n    Ok((\n        Outcome {\n            stdout,\n            stderr,\n            code: status.code(),\n            signal: status.signal(),\n        },\n        elapsed,\n    ))\n}","new_string":"/// What one unbounded-stdin run observed.\npub struct UnboundedRun {\n    pub outcome: Outcome,\n    pub elapsed: std::time::Duration,\n    /// Bytes the feeder managed to push into the child's stdin before it exited.\n    ///\n    /// This is the load-bearing measurement: `scanf` is lazy, so a faithful\n    /// implementation accepts at most a couple of buffers (plus whatever the\n    /// 64 KiB pipe holds), whereas one that reads to end-of-file first swallows\n    /// gigabytes. The gap is about six orders of magnitude, which makes this a\n    /// far sharper signal than wall-clock time.\n    pub bytes_fed: u64,\n}\n\n/// Run `exe` against a stdin that **never reaches end-of-file**: a background\n/// thread writes `pattern` in a loop until the child goes away.\n///\n/// Returns `Err(elapsed)` if the child had to be killed, so a hang cannot block\n/// the suite forever.\npub fn run_unbounded(\n    exe: &Path,\n    pattern: &[u8],\n    timeout: std::time::Duration,\n) -> Result<UnboundedRun, std::time::Duration> {\n    let mut child = Command::new(exe)\n        .stdin(Stdio::piped())\n        .stdout(Stdio::piped())\n        .stderr(Stdio::piped())\n        .spawn()\n        .unwrap_or_else(|e| panic!(\"spawn {exe:?}: {e}\"));\n\n    let mut sink = child.stdin.take().expect(\"piped stdin\");\n    let block: Vec<u8> = pattern.repeat(4096 / pattern.len().max(1) + 1);\n    let fed = std::sync::Arc::new(AtomicU64::new(0));\n    let fed_writer = std::sync::Arc::clone(&fed);\n    let feeder = std::thread::spawn(move || {\n        // Stops as soon as the reader is gone (EPIPE).\n        while sink.write_all(&block).is_ok() {\n            fed_writer.fetch_add(block.len() as u64, Ordering::Relaxed);\n        }\n    });\n\n    let start = std::time::Instant::now();\n    let status = loop {\n        match child.try_wait().expect(\"try_wait\") {\n            Some(s) => break s,\n            None => {\n                if start.elapsed() > timeout {\n                    let _ = child.kill();\n                    let _ = child.wait();\n                    let _ = feeder.join();\n                    return Err(start.elapsed());\n                }\n                std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(2));\n            }\n        }\n    };\n    let elapsed = start.elapsed();\n    let bytes_fed = fed.load(Ordering::Relaxed);\n\n    let mut stdout = Vec::new();\n    let mut stderr = Vec::new();\n    if let Some(mut s) = child.stdout.take() {\n        let _ = s.read_to_end(&mut stdout);\n    }\n    if let Some(mut s) = child.stderr.take() {\n        let _ = s.read_to_end(&mut stderr);\n    }\n    let _ = feeder.join();\n\n    Ok(UnboundedRun {\n        outcome: Outcome {\n            stdout,\n            stderr,\n            code: status.code(),\n            signal: status.signal(),\n        },\n        elapsed,\n        bytes_fed,\n    })\n}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_read_input_tokens":164093,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":552,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c25b394-7046-4ff6-8cec-46c32ba03643","uuid":"557c8d6f-0841-4fea-ae9d-5e45361d2178","timestamp":"2026-08-18T13:57:51.923Z"}
