5 |` or `cat /dev/zero |`, C exits instantly while Rust burned 3–4 s allocating gigabytes, only terminating because `read_to_end` eventually returned `OutOfMemory`. On a memory-capped host it would have been OOM-killed — a different exit status. Fixed by putting the scanner directly on `BufRead::fill_buf`/`consume`, which is precisely the peek-then-commit primitive `scanf` implements with `ungetc`.\n\n**2. `SIGPIPE` was left ignored.** The Rust runtime installs `SIG_IGN` before `main`; a C program starts at `SIG_DFL`. Writing to a reader-less pipe: C dies with signal 13, Rust exited **0**. Fixed with `restore_default_sigpipe()` in the binary's `main` only — deliberately *not* in the `.so`'s `main` export, since the C `main` doesn't touch signal dispositions either.\n\n## Two harness bugs that were producing false passes\n\nI caught both by mutation testing rather than by inspection:\n\n- **Stale artifacts.** `cargo test --test <name>` doesn't rebuild `example` targets, so the FFI tests `dlopen`ed a leftover `.so` and **passed against an injected `^`-instead-of-`|` bug**. A stale `target/release/driver` separately made the SIGPIPE row pass while the fix was absent. `assert_fresh` now hard-fails on any artifact older than its sources.\n- **fd-1 interleaving.** Capturing `printf` output means redirecting a process-wide descriptor; the test harness writes progress lines to it from other threads. Each capturing test now runs in a dedicated single-threaded subprocess.\n\n## Why the check marks mean something\n\n`scripts/negative_control.sh` injects 11 realistic translation bugs and requires each to be rejected. The eager-stdin mutant **survived the first run** — `cfg30` asserted wall-clock `< 5 s` and the mutant finished in 3–4 s. I replaced that with an assertion on *bytes consumed from the endless stream* (`< 1 MiB`), where lazy vs. eager differ by six orders of magnitude instead of a factor of two.\n\n## Final state\n\n| gate | result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff | **empty** (`driver`, `main`); 0 unresolved symbols |\n| `CONFIGS.md` — 44 rows | all pass, 0 unchecked |\n| `ERRORS.md` — 22 rows | all pass, each asserting agreement **and** the hand-derived C value |\n| feature combinations | 1 (no `[features]`, no `#if`, no CMake `option()`) — derived as a power set, not hard-coded |\n| profiles | dev + release (`panic = \"abort\"`) |\n\nOne extra finding worth noting: `cfg43` confirms the C reference behaves identically at `-O0` and `-O2`, so \"C is ground truth\" is unambiguous here and the expected values aren't pinned to one particular build. `c_src/` was never modified (original mtime and checksum intact).","ttft_ms":4846,"ttft_stream_ms":4690,"time_to_request_ms":36,"type":"result","duration_ms":2283451,"uuid":"531ae655-beb1-4f9f-889e-e63d200734a3"}
